= Zeigner

On 21 March the Saxon Landtag elects Erich Zeigner Minister-President. He is thirty-six, a former judge, and the most left-wing head of government in Germany. He talks in public about the Reichswehr's secret arms stores and the industrialists who pay the nationalist leagues. [? if saxony_government = 1 : Our ministers keep their seats in his cabinet, and he asks only that the party stop calling his colleagues traitors. ?][? if saxony_government = 0 : He needs our votes. In return he offers an amnesty, legal standing for the control committees, and a blind eye to the hundreds. ?]

- @tolerate: Keep Zeigner in office, on our conditions.
- @refuse: Refuse him our votes.

@tolerate
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The hundreds march openly in Saxony. The Reichswehr starts a file.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids keeping Social Democrats in office.
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.against('united_front');
RG.district('saxony', {guards: 1.5, loyalty: 6, members: 0.05});
RG.ecci('radek', 3);
Q.e23_zeigner = 1;
Q.spd_relation += 5;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

The agreement is signed in Dresden. The control committees become legal bodies, and the hundreds parade in Leipzig, Chemnitz and Plauen.

@refuse
subtitle: Zeigner turns to the Democrats, and Saxony's workers blame us.
on-arrival: {!
RG.ecci('radek', -4);
RG.district('saxony', {loyalty: -6});
Q.e23_zeigner = 2;
Q.saxony_government = 0;
Q.spd_relation -= 7;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

[? if e23_had_sax = 1 : Our ministers resign. ?] Zeigner governs with the Democrats, and the Saxon SPD stops inviting our speakers to its meetings.
